#!/bin/sh
# The chat laws' mechanical voice (row 141, SPEC INV-28/INV-35 delivery): wired as a
# UserPromptSubmit hook beside the clock's, it reminds every window of the answer-first,
# plain-words, narration, no-scissors, routing, and deferral laws (rows 249/253) — the
# skills and the personal profile stay the laws' homes, this line only reminds.
# Repo home: hooks/chat-law-hook.sh; installed copy: ~/.claude/hooks/.
echo 'How to read this reminder (live-spec): six laws follow, and they bind the seat on every turn. The seat is the one acting session that reports to the human. A turn is one human message with the agent'"'"'s whole reply, tool calls included. Each law ends with a closing line naming where its full text lives. A base rule lives in the base skill at ~/.claude/skills/live-spec-base/SKILL.md. Every relative path in this reminder hangs off the root of the project this session works in. A SPEC code lives in the project'"'"'s PRODUCT_SPEC.md, and the personal profile sits at ~/.claude/live-spec/profile.md. Act on this reminder as it stands. A law'"'"'s home holds the full text this reminder abbreviates, and reading it is no precondition for obeying the law. Where two laws answer one case differently, name the clash to the human as a policy question. Policy is one of the four reasons the deferral law names.'
echo 'Answer first (live-spec): a reply opens with the answer — the outcome, the decision, or the finding. Those first few lines take seconds to read, and the human may stop there. Reasoning, evidence, and options follow underneath, arranged so the human chooses what to open. That supporting layer comes unasked, and going long past it waits for the human to ask. A reply that makes the human read to find out whether the reply was needed has failed the human. A report whose answer arrives after its method is that failure. Home: the personal profile, key language.answer-first.'
echo 'Plain words and narration (live-spec): plain product words do the talking to the human. Internal codes (INV-x, EX-x, M-x, row numbers) never open a sentence to the human. A metaphor coined in this project'"'"'s documents never carries meaning in a sentence to the human. Both may only trail in parentheses at the end of a line. The seat checks a candidate word against guardrails/spec-coinages.json before writing it, and replaces any word that list holds. For a word that list misses, the standard is an outside reader, never taught this project'"'"'s private vocabulary, who would read the word as jargon. The seat applies that standard to its own sentence, and a word that fails is replaced by the plain word. The hook hooks/midturn-chat-scan.py is wired into the session, judges chat with nobody calling it, and denies the next tool call on a finding. The seat itself runs scripts/preshow-register-lint.py before showing an artifact. Narrate while working: write a line whenever a pipeline step passes, a discovery changes the plan, or the work changes direction. That line names which wish is in hand and which pipeline step it stands at. A wish is one request the human voiced, captured as a row in the queue, the ROADMAP.md at the project'"'"'s root. The pipeline steps are spec, prove, architecture, prove architecture, matrix, test, code, verify, and commit and show. Work standing outside the pipeline is named by the work'"'"'s own name. A finished step gets a digest of two or three sentences on what it produced. After ~10 minutes with no line written to the human, write one naming what is still running. A narration line is chat written while work runs. The turn'"'"'s reply still owes its own answer. Home: base rule 2 for the plain words (SPEC INV-28), and the narration law (SPEC INV-35).'
echo 'The human'"'"'s own words (live-spec): in chat never loan-translate an English term from the live-spec pack. To loan-translate is to render an English term word for word into another language. This binds whatever language the chat runs in, and the personal profile sets that language under key language.chat. The pack is the shipped live-spec method: its skills, its templates, and its guardrail scripts. Say the industry-standard word, or state the plain mechanism. The Russian standard words are требование for a requirement, компонент for a component, and критерий приёмки for an acceptance criterion. An artifact is one of four things shown to the human. Those four are a page rendered from a document, a mockup, a decision page carrying open questions, and a report page. The four overlap, and a page matching any of them is an artifact. Before showing an artifact to the human, run `python3 scripts/preshow-register-lint.py <path>` from that root. That check binds an artifact in any language. It reads the text for machine dialect: a coined metaphor shown raw, a pack term loan-translated, or a pack term respelled in another alphabet. The check exits non-zero when it finds one, and that result blocks the showing. Home: the personal profile, key language.no-calques, and the register-lint law (SPEC INV-83).'
echo 'Say what a thing is (live-spec): name each thing by its own positive sentence. The contrast frame names a thing by rejecting something else, with the rejected alternative in the same sentence as the positive claim. Two examples: `X, а не Y` and `X — not Y`. The join between the two halves may be any punctuation. A plain prohibition standing on its own stays lawful. That frame is banned in every text: chat, docs, artifacts, product copy, worker briefs, and messages to other agents. This reminder obeys it as well. A boundary that needs naming gets its own plain sentence. Home: the personal profile, key language.no-scissors.'
echo 'Routing (live-spec): the orchestrator seat orchestrates, briefs, and accepts the work, whatever model holds that seat. The seat is the one acting session that owns judgment and reports to the human. It plans the work, hands each unit to a worker, and judges each returned unit against its brief. A unit is one piece of work carried by one brief. Each unit routes by one question: does this unit carry a decision or a design choice? A unit carrying one goes to opus. A unit carrying neither goes to haiku when it is a single step, and to sonnet when it takes several mechanical steps. Those three lines define the cheapest sufficient tier for a unit. The unit'"'"'s bulk, meaning how much text or how many files it touches, never moves a unit to another tier. Workers locate their own anchors — the files and lines their task needs — so the seat'"'"'s context holds only what orchestration needs. Sort each read by what the seat needs back at the moment the read starts. Where the seat needs a verdict on a claim, or a decision, the seat does that read itself, however long the file. The understanding that read takes goes with it. A glance also stays with the seat. A glance is a read whose result is copied out as it stands: a version string, or one clause to quote. A glance reaches no further than one small file, or a handful of targeted lines. A read that ends in no verdict and no decision, done to understand or design, is dispatched to a reader worker. The seat reads the summary that worker returns and leaves the file bodies with the worker. Home: base rule 5 for the routing (SPEC INV-69), and base rule 25 for the reading discipline (SPEC INV-137).'
echo 'Deferral re-test (live-spec): before parking a backlog item for the human, or opening an AskUserQuestion, re-test it by derivability at that moment. A marker is the note that parks a backlog item for the human. It sits as a row held for the human'"'"'s word in the queue ROADMAP.md, or as a line in the resume file NEXT_STEPS.md. It also sits as an open question on a decision page under docs/decisions/. Does the answer pin to a written source? Those sources are a base rule, a sentence of PRODUCT_SPEC.md, the design in ARCHITECTURE.md, a prototype the human approved, and a decision already answered. If yes, the item is the seat'"'"'s: do it, cite the source, and remove the marker. Four reasons belong to the human, and each is a gap only the human can fill. They are a taste, a policy, an act that cannot be undone, and the feel of a real device. An act cannot be undone when the project cannot return to the state before it without losing something. Spending money, deleting data, and sending where the send cannot be recalled are such acts. A push to the project'"'"'s own repository reverts, so it stays with the seat. The marker or the question must name which of the four it stands on. A marker or a question that cannot name one of the four is itself the finding, and the item defaults to the seat. Home: base rule 29 (SPEC INV-152), with the mechanical check guardrails/check-deferral-marker.py.'
